---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'August 2, 2026';
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Framewrite"
  description="How Framewrite collects, uses, and shares data -- for account holders and for the anonymous free-trial upload."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <article class="legal">
    <div class="container legal-inner">
      <p class="legal-meta">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

      <div class="legal-body">
        <p>
          This policy covers <strong>Framewrite</strong> (framewrite.cc and app.framewrite.cc) --
          both accounts you sign up for and the anonymous, no-login free trial on this site. If
          you have questions about anything here, email
          <a href="mailto:contact@framewrite.cc">contact@framewrite.cc</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>If you create an account</strong>, we collect your email address, display name,
          and profile picture from Google Sign-In; any video or audio you upload and the
          document/transcript we generate from it; API keys you create; feedback you submit; and,
          if you connect Google Drive, an authorization token that lets us save documents there on
          your behalf (kept encrypted, and only used for that purpose).
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>If you use the free trial</strong> (no account required), we collect the video
          or audio file you upload, the document we generate from it, and your IP address --
          the IP address is used only to enforce a daily limit on free trials and is not tied to
          any account. See <a href="#turnstile">Cloudflare Turnstile</a> below for the bot-check
          step the trial uses.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Billing</strong>: wallet top-ups are handled by Stripe. We never see or store
          your card number -- we keep a Stripe customer ID and a ledger of charges/top-ups/refunds
          in cents.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>On this marketing site</strong>, we use Google Analytics to understand traffic
          and which pages/features get used (page views and a small number of named events, like
          starting or finishing a free-trial upload). No account-identifying information is sent
          to Analytics from this site.
        </p>

        <h2>How your upload gets processed</h2>
        <p>
          Turning a video or audio file into a document requires sending parts of it to
          specialized third-party services, whether you're signed in or using the free trial:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Transcription</strong> -- your audio is sent to a speech-to-text/diarization
            provider to produce a speaker-tagged transcript.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Frame analysis and document composition</strong> -- for video, extracted
            frames (e.g. slides, diagrams, tables) are sent to AI providers to
            classify what's on screen and to write the final document from your transcript.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          These providers process this data to perform the service on our behalf; we don't
          authorize them to use it to train their own models beyond what their own terms specify
          for API customers.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep things</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Account documents</strong> are kept for 7 days after processing, after which the
          file itself is deleted (your job history and billing record are kept, since that's part
          of your account's usage history) -- download what you need before then.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Free-trial uploads and documents</strong> are deleted entirely, record and all,
          within about 6 hours of submission. There's no way to retrieve a trial result after
          that, and no way for us to look one up by request, since nothing ties it to you.
        </p>

        <h2 id="turnstile">Cloudflare Turnstile</h2>
        <p>
          The free trial's upload form is protected by
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/products/turnstile/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Cloudflare Turnstile
          </a>, which checks that a submission is coming from a real browser rather than a script,
          without a visible puzzle in most cases. Using the trial sends some data about your
          browser/device to Cloudflare for this check. Cloudflare's handling of that data is
          governed by their own privacy policy and Turnstile-specific addendum, not by us:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/en-gb/turnstile-privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              Cloudflare Turnstile Privacy Policy Addendum
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              Cloudflare Privacy Policy
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What we store in your browser</h2>
        <p>
          The app keeps your sign-in session in your browser's local storage (so you don't have to
          log in every visit). The free-trial widget on this site saves the id of your most recent
          trial upload locally, purely so reloading the page can show you its progress again
          instead of losing track of it -- it's cleared automatically once that upload finishes or
          expires. Neither of these are cookies, and neither is shared with anyone.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can download or delete your documents at any time from your dashboard. To request
          deletion of your account and associated data, or to ask what data we hold about you,
          email <a href="mailto:contact@framewrite.cc">contact@framewrite.cc</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>Framewrite isn't directed at, and isn't knowingly used by, children under 13.</p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes in a way that matters, we'll update the date at the top of this
          page. Continued use of Framewrite after a change means you accept the update.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions, requests, or concerns about any of the above:
          <a href="mailto:contact@framewrite.cc">contact@framewrite.cc</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</MarketingLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding: 56px 0 72px;
  }

  .legal-inner {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .legal-meta {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-4);
    margin: 0 0 32px;
    padding-bottom: 32px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .legal-body {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .legal-body p,
  .legal-body ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.4em;
  }

  .legal-body ul {
    padding-left: 1.3em;
  }

  .legal-body li {
    margin-bottom: 0.6em;
  }

  .legal-body h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin: 1.6em 0 0.6em;
  }

  .legal-body a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
